    "text": "Congestion Detection: Multiplicative Decrease: If congestion occurs, the congestion window size must be decreased. > The only way the sender can guess that congestion has occurred is by the need to retransmit a segment. > Retransmission can occur when a timer times out or when three ACKs are received. 1. If a time-out occurs, there is a stronger possibility of congestion; a segment has probably been dropped in the network. a. TCP sets value of threshold to one-half of the current window size. b. Sets cwnd to the size of one segment. c. Starts the slow-start phase again.",
